;
;The DC brush motors require a minimum voltage for any motion to be
;generated.   The Pwm Offset value is added to positive Pwm commands and
;is subtracted from negative Pwm commands.  The PwmOffset eliminates most
;of the "deadband" in the motor/ amplifier system.  The offset is set to 
;a value that is about 75% of the actual voltage offset measured.  The 
;equation is:   PwmOffset = 0.75 * Voffset * Maximum Pwm Cnt / Vbus
;
; Pwm Offset For X,Y,Z,W Axis
00000000025 ; 140
;
;In order to prevent drive amplifier overheating, a software simulation of
;motor load is continuously run to predict amplifier temperature.  This 
;parameter (Load Integrator Limit) sets the allowable predicted temperature
;limit, above which an alarm will be posted and the drive system shut down.
;
; Pwm Amp Load Integrator Limit
